[2026-03-14T22:38:15.953Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_013EXxEd8gEwRWUcDgFpSnba","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Users can install it globally, record sessions, upload recordings, and manage them through command-line commands.\n\n## Key Installation & Setup\n\nInstall via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun globally. Authentication requires creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Primary Commands\n\nThe main operations include:\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launches Replay Browser to record a session (defaults to `about:blank`)\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Uploads recordings; without arguments opens an interactive menu\n- **`replayio list`** - Shows all local recordings with ID, host, date, duration, and status\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manages account authentication\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Deletes recordings (supports `-a, --all` flag)\n- **`replayio update`** - Updates the Replay Browser component\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n\"Record your application to gather performance data\" by running `replayio record https://myapp.com`, then upload the session. If manual upload is needed later, use `replayio upload <recording-id>`.\n\nAdditional features include `upload-source-maps` for workspace source map management and integration with Replay's MCP Server for debugging recorded applications through Claude."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bb98dc9-6ec8-4f0f-afd1-551c13e4f5cd","uuid":"844e5249-4604-4fcc-af24-89ceb0c211fa","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4854,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay CLI Documentation\n\n**Replay CLI** is a tool for recording application sessions to gather performance data and debug issues. Users can install it globally, record sessions, upload recordings, and manage them through command-line commands.\n\n## Key Installation & Setup\n\nInstall via npm, yarn, pnpm, or bun globally. Authentication requires creating an API key at https://app.replay.io settings and storing it in the `REPLAY_API_KEY` environment variable.\n\n## Primary Commands\n\nThe main operations include:\n\n- **`replayio record [url]`** - Launches Replay Browser to record a session (defaults to `about:blank`)\n- **`replayio upload [ids...]`** - Uploads recordings; without arguments opens an interactive menu\n- **`replayio list`** - Shows all local recordings with ID, host, date, duration, and status\n- **`replayio login/logout`** - Manages account authentication\n- **`replayio remove [ids...]`** - Deletes recordings (supports `-a, --all` flag)\n- **`replayio update`** - Updates the Replay Browser component\n\n## Typical Workflow\n\n\"Record your application to gather performance data\" by running `replayio record https://myapp.com`, then upload the session. If manual upload is needed later, use `replayio upload <recording-id>`.\n\nAdditional features include `upload-source-maps` for workspace source map management and integration with Replay's MCP Server for debugging recorded applications through Claude.","durationMs":3518,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-cli/SKILL.md"}}
[2026-03-14T22:38:16.212Z] {"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Uzk2ujyqEioLtEo9Hab36m","type":"tool_result","content":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution histories. According to the documentation, \"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\"\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nThe tool provides two main categories of functionality:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred and when, including error identification, timeline analysis, and source code investigation.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened, using dependency tracking and detailed state inspection to understand cause-and-effect relationships.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured approach: frame questions, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, apply explanatory tools to understand causation, form hypotheses supported by gathered data, and explain conclusions with evidence.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nTwo fundamental terms organize the recording data: \"Points\" represent specific execution moments when JS statements run, and \"Elements\" reference particular DOM elements independent of any specific point in time."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4bb98dc9-6ec8-4f0f-afd1-551c13e4f5cd","uuid":"2bf8d38e-fddd-458f-81cd-fdcba26ce67c","tool_use_result":{"bytes":4555,"code":200,"codeText":"OK","result":"# Replay MCP Overview\n\nReplay MCP is a tool for inspecting Replay.io recordings, which capture complete browser execution histories. According to the documentation, \"The recording is essentially a gigantic database containing everything that happened while the app executed.\"\n\n## Key Capabilities\n\nThe tool provides two main categories of functionality:\n\n**Exploratory Tools** help discover what occurred and when, including error identification, timeline analysis, and source code investigation.\n\n**Explanatory Tools** clarify why events happened, using dependency tracking and detailed state inspection to understand cause-and-effect relationships.\n\n## Investigation Methodology\n\nThe documentation recommends a structured approach: frame questions, use exploratory tools to identify relevant events, apply explanatory tools to understand causation, form hypotheses supported by gathered data, and explain conclusions with evidence.\n\n## Core Concepts\n\nTwo fundamental terms organize the recording data: \"Points\" represent specific execution moments when JS statements run, and \"Elements\" reference particular DOM elements independent of any specific point in time.","durationMs":2796,"url":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/replayio/skills/refs/heads/main/skills/replay-mcp/SKILL.md"}}
